{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "def sort_matrix(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a matrix by the sum of its rows in ascending order.\n    Returns a new matrix with rows sorted based on their sums.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_row_sum(row: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper to calculate the arithmetic sum of elements in a row.\"\"\"\n        return sum(row)\n\n    # Pair each row with its calculated sum\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        rows_with_sums.append((_calculate_row_sum(row), row))\n\n    # Sort the pairs based on the row sum (the first element of the tuple)\n    sorted_rows_with_sums = sorted(rows_with_sums, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    # Extract only the sorted rows from the pairs\n    sorted_matrix = [row for _, row in sorted_rows_with_sums]\n\n    return sorted_matrix"}
