{"task_id": "Mbpp/16", "solution": "def text_lowercase_underscore(input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the input string contains sequences of lowercase letters\n    joined with an underscore, returning True if it does and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def is_lowercase_letter(char: str) -> bool:\n        return 'a' <= char <= 'z'\n\n    def contains_only_valid_chars(s: str) -> bool:\n        for char in s:\n            if not (is_lowercase_letter(char) or char == '_'):\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def check_underscore_placement(s: str) -> bool:\n        if s.startswith('_') or s.endswith('_'):\n            return False\n        if '__' in s:\n            return False\n        return True\n\n    def validate_pattern_segments(s: str) -> bool:\n        parts = s.split('_')\n        for part in parts:\n            # Each part must consist entirely of lowercase letters\n            for char in part:\n                if not is_lowercase_letter(char):\n                    return False\n        return True\n\n    if not input_string:\n        return False\n\n    # The pattern explicitly states \"joined with an underscore\", implying at least one underscore must exist.\n    if '_' not in input_string:\n        return False\n\n    # Validate all characters are either lowercase letters or underscores\n    if not contains_only_valid_chars(input_string):\n        return False\n\n    # Validate underscore placement (no leading, trailing, or consecutive underscores)\n    if not check_underscore_placement(input_string):\n        return False\n\n    # Validate that the segments between underscores are valid sequences of lowercase letters\n    if not validate_pattern_segments(input_string):\n        return False\n\n    return True"}
