{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Bell number for a given non-negative integer n.\n    This represents the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    bell = [0] * (n + 1)\n    bell[0] = 1\n\n    def combinations(n_val, k_val):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient (n_val choose k_val).\"\"\"\n        if k_val < 0 or k_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if k_val == 0 or k_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if k_val > n_val // 2:\n            k_val = n_val - k_val\n\n        res = 1\n        for i in range(k_val):\n            res = res * (n_val - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    # Compute Bell numbers using the recurrence: B_i = sum_{k=0 to i-1} (i-1 choose k) * B_k\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        current_bell_sum = 0\n        for k in range(i):\n            current_bell_sum += combinations(i - 1, k) * bell[k]\n        bell[i] = current_bell_sum\n\n    return bell[n]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number, representing the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\n    It uses dynamic programming based on the Bell triangle construction.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a 2D list (Bell triangle) to store intermediate values.\n    # dp[i][j] will store the j-th value in the i-th row of the triangle.\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # The base case for the Bell triangle is dp[0][0] = 1.\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Bell triangle using the recurrence relations.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of the current row (dp[i][0]) is the last element\n        # of the previous row (dp[i-1][i-1]).\n        dp[i][0] = dp[i - 1][i - 1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Each subsequent element in the row is the sum of the element to its left\n            # and the element diagonally above and to its left.\n            dp[i][j] = dp[i][j - 1] + dp[i - 1][j - 1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row (0-indexed).\n    return dp[n][0]"}
