{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "def is_sublist(main_list: list, sublist: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list contains the given sublist as a contiguous sequence.\n    Returns True if the sublist is found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sublist)\n\n    if m == 0:\n        return True  # An empty list is always considered a sublist.\n    if m > n:\n        return False # A sublist cannot be longer than the main list.\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        # Check if the segment main_list[i : i+m] matches sublist\n        match = True\n        for j in range(m):\n            if main_list[i + j] != sublist[j]:\n                match = False\n                break\n        if match:\n            return True\n\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "def is_sublist(main_list, sublist):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list contains the given sublist as a contiguous subsequence.\n    Returns True if the sublist is found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    len_main = len(main_list)\n    len_sub = len(sublist)\n\n    if len_sub == 0:\n        return True  # An empty sublist is always considered a contiguous sublist.\n\n    if len_sub > len_main:\n        return False # A sublist cannot be longer than the main list.\n\n    # Iterate through the main_list to find a potential starting point for the sublist\n    for i in range(len_main - len_sub + 1):\n        match = True\n        # Check if the slice of main_list matches the sublist\n        for j in range(len_sub):\n            if main_list[i + j] != sublist[j]:\n                match = False\n                break\n        if match:\n            return True # Found a contiguous match\n\n    return False"}
