{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "def comb_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers using the comb sort algorithm with a shrink factor of 1.3.\n    It sorts the list in ascending order while preserving all elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    gap = n\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        # Calculate new gap using the shrink factor\n        gap = max(1, int(gap / 1.3))\n        swapped = False\n\n        # Perform a modified bubble sort for the current gap\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                swapped = True\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "def comb_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements using the comb sort algorithm.\n    It sorts the list in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    arr = list(input_list)  # Create a mutable copy to avoid modifying the original list\n\n    gap = n\n    swapped = True\n    GAP_FACTOR = 1.3\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        # Calculate the next gap value\n        gap = int(gap / GAP_FACTOR)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1\n\n        swapped = False\n\n        # Perform a single pass with the current gap\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                swapped = True\n    return arr"}
