{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using an iterative approach.\n    The sequence is defined by P(1) = 1, P(2) = 1, and P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        # As per instructions, assume n is a valid positive integer.\n        # This branch would typically raise an error but is omitted.\n        pass\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a list to store sequence numbers, using 1-based indexing.\n    # P[k] will store the k-th Newman-Conway number.\n    P = [0] * (n + 1)\n    P[1] = 1\n    P[2] = 1\n\n    # Compute sequence numbers iteratively up to n.\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        P[i] = P[P[i - 1]] + P[i - P[i - 1]]\n\n    return P[n]"}
