{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "def decimal_to_binary(decimal: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a decimal integer to its binary equivalent as a string with no leading zeros.\n    The conversion uses the standard division-by-2 algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    if decimal == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    binary_digits = []\n    while decimal > 0:\n        remainder = decimal % 2\n        binary_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        decimal //= 2\n\n    # The digits are collected in reverse order, so we reverse the list before joining.\n    return \"\".join(binary_digits[::-1])"}
