{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m) using a recursive approach with memoization.\n    Eulerian numbers count permutations of {1, ..., n} with exactly m ascents.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _eulerian_recursive(n_val, m_val):\n        # Base cases:\n        # A(n, m) = 0 if m < 0 or m >= n\n        if m_val < 0 or m_val >= n_val:\n            return 0\n        # A(0, 0) = 1\n        if n_val == 0 and m_val == 0:\n            return 1\n\n        # Check memoization table\n        if (n_val, m_val) in memo:\n            return memo[(n_val, m_val)]\n\n        # Recurrence relation: A(n, m) = (m + 1) * A(n-1, m) + (n - m) * A(n-1, m-1)\n        result = (m_val + 1) * _eulerian_recursive(n_val - 1, m_val) + \\\n                 (n_val - m_val) * _eulerian_recursive(n_val - 1, m_val - 1)\n\n        # Store result in memoization table\n        memo[(n_val, m_val)] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _eulerian_recursive(n, m)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m), which is the number of permutations of {1, ..., n} with m ascents.\n    The formula used is A(n, m) = sum_{k=0}^{m} (-1)^k * C(n+1, k) * (m - k + 1)^n.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def combinations(N, K):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(N, K), 'N choose K'.\"\"\"\n        if K < 0 or K > N:\n            return 0\n        if K == 0 or K == N:\n            return 1\n        if K > N // 2:\n            K = N - K\n        \n        res = 1\n        for i in range(K):\n            res = res * (N - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    def power(base, exp):\n        \"\"\"Calculates base raised to the power of exp (base^exp).\"\"\"\n        if exp < 0:\n            return 0 \n        if exp == 0:\n            return 1\n        \n        result = 1\n        current_base = base\n        current_exp = exp\n        while current_exp > 0:\n            if current_exp % 2 == 1:\n                result *= current_base\n            current_base *= current_base\n            current_exp //= 2\n        return result\n    \n    # Handle mathematical edge cases for n and m as per standard definitions\n    if m < 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 if m == 0 else 0\n\n    eulerian_sum = 0\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        term = power(-1, k) * combinations(n + 1, k) * power(m - k + 1, n)\n        eulerian_sum += term\n        \n    return eulerian_sum"}
