{"task_id": "Mbpp/129", "solution": "def magic_square_test(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given square matrix is a magic square.\n    It verifies if all row, column, and diagonal sums are equal.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def validate_input(matrix):\n        # As per instructions, isinstance checks and exceptions are omitted.\n        pass\n\n    def validate_square_matrix(matrix):\n        # As per instructions, isinstance checks and exceptions are omitted.\n        pass\n\n    def calculate_row_sums(matrix):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of each row in the matrix.\"\"\"\n        return [sum(row) for row in matrix]\n\n    def calculate_column_sums(matrix):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of each column in the matrix.\"\"\"\n        n = len(matrix)\n        column_sums = [0] * n\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(n):\n                column_sums[j] += matrix[i][j]\n        return column_sums\n\n    def calculate_main_diagonal_sum(matrix):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the main diagonal (top-left to bottom-right).\"\"\"\n        n = len(matrix)\n        main_diag_sum = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            main_diag_sum += matrix[i][i]\n        return main_diag_sum\n\n    def calculate_anti_diagonal_sum(matrix):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the anti-diagonal (top-right to bottom-left).\"\"\"\n        n = len(matrix)\n        anti_diag_sum = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            anti_diag_sum += matrix[i][n - 1 - i]\n        return anti_diag_sum\n\n    def verify_all_sums_equal(row_sums, col_sums, main_diag, anti_diag):\n        \"\"\"Verifies that all calculated sums are equal.\"\"\"\n        if not row_sums: # Handle empty matrix case implicitly, though design implies non-empty.\n            return True\n\n        expected_sum = row_sums[0]\n\n        # Check all row sums\n        if not all(s == expected_sum for s in row_sums):\n            return False\n\n        # Check all column sums\n        if not all(s == expected_sum for s in col_sums):\n            return False\n\n        # Check main diagonal sum\n        if main_diag != expected_sum:\n            return False\n\n        # Check anti-diagonal sum\n        if anti_diag != expected_sum:\n            return False\n\n        return True\n\n    validate_input(matrix)\n    validate_square_matrix(matrix)\n\n    if not matrix:\n        return True # An empty matrix can be considered a trivial magic square if all sums are vacuously equal.\n    \n    n = len(matrix)\n    if n == 0 or any(len(row) != n for row in matrix):\n        # This implicitly handles non-square or empty inner lists,\n        # adhering to no explicit exceptions/isinstance for output code.\n        return False\n\n    row_sums = calculate_row_sums(matrix)\n    col_sums = calculate_column_sums(matrix)\n    main_diag_sum = calculate_main_diagonal_sum(matrix)\n    anti_diag_sum = calculate_anti_diagonal_sum(matrix)\n\n    return verify_all_sums_equal(row_sums, col_sums, main_diag_sum, anti_diag_sum)"}
