{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return arr[:]\n\n    # Helper function to reverse elements from index 0 to i (inclusive).\n    def flip(sub_arr, i):\n        start = 0\n        while start < i:\n            sub_arr[start], sub_arr[i] = sub_arr[i], sub_arr[start]\n            start += 1\n            i -= 1\n\n    # Helper function to find the index of the maximum element in sub_arr[0...size-1].\n    def find_max_index(sub_arr, size):\n        max_val = sub_arr[0]\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, size):\n            if sub_arr[i] > max_val:\n                max_val = sub_arr[i]\n                max_idx = i\n        return max_idx\n\n    # Create a copy of the input list to perform sorting.\n    sorted_arr = arr[:]\n\n    # Iterate from the end of the list (largest unsorted portion) down to 2.\n    # 'curr_size' represents the length of the currently unsorted prefix.\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted prefix.\n        max_idx = find_max_index(sorted_arr, curr_size)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct final position\n        # within the current unsorted prefix (i.e., at index curr_size - 1).\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # If the maximum element is not at the beginning, flip it to the beginning.\n            if max_idx != 0:\n                flip(sorted_arr, max_idx)\n\n            # Flip the entire unsorted prefix to move the maximum element from the beginning\n            # to its correct position at the end of the unsorted prefix.\n            flip(sorted_arr, curr_size - 1)\n\n    return sorted_arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def flip(arr: list, k: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses elements in the list from index 0 up to index k (inclusive).\n    Modifies the list in-place.\n    \"\"\"\n    start = 0\n    end = k\n    while start < end:\n        arr[start], arr[end] = arr[end], arr[start]\n        start += 1\n        end -= 1\n\ndef find_max_index(arr: list, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the maximum element in the sub-array arr[0...n-1].\n    Returns the index of the largest element.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_idx = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if arr[i] > arr[max_idx]:\n            max_idx = i\n    return max_idx\n\ndef pancake_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list with elements sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list in-place\n    new_arr = list(arr)\n\n    # Start from the complete array and reduce its size one by one\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current sub-array new_arr[0...current_size-1]\n        max_idx = find_max_index(new_arr, current_size)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct position\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            # Move the maximum element to the beginning of the sub-array if it's not already there\n            if max_idx != 0:\n                flip(new_arr, max_idx)\n            # Move the maximum element from the beginning to its correct position at the end of the sub-array\n            flip(new_arr, current_size - 1)\n            \n    return new_arr"}
