{"task_id": "Mbpp/167", "solution": "```python\ndef next_power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the smallest power of 2 greater than or equal to n.\n    Handles n=0 by returning 1 as a special case.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Decrement n to handle cases where n is already a power of 2,\n    # and to prepare for finding the next power of 2 using bit manipulation.\n    n -= 1\n\n    # Set all bits to 1 that are to the right of the most significant bit.\n    # This efficiently propagates the highest set bit downwards.\n    n |= n >> 1\n    n |= n >> 2\n    n |= n >> 4\n    n |= n >> 8\n    n |= n >> 16\n    n |= n >> 32\n\n    # Incrementing the resulting number (which is now 2^k - 1)\n    # yields the smallest power of 2 greater than or equal to the original n.\n    return n + 1\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "def find_even_pair(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of pairs of integers in a list that XOR to an even number.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):  # Generate unique pairs (i, j) where i < j\n            xor_result = numbers[i] ^ numbers[j]\n            if xor_result % 2 == 0:  # Check if the XOR result is even\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
