{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef is_majority(sorted_array: List[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    def binary_search_first(arr: List[int], target: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of the target in a sorted array.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                high = mid - 1  # Look for an earlier occurrence in the left half\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    def binary_search_last(arr: List[int], target: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of the target in a sorted array.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                low = mid + 1  # Look for a later occurrence in the right half\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    first_idx = binary_search_first(sorted_array, element)\n\n    # If the element is not found, it cannot be a majority element\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = binary_search_last(sorted_array, element)\n\n    # Calculate the count of the element\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    # Check if the count is greater than n/2\n    return count > (n / 2)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/227", "solution": "def min_of_three(num1, num2, num3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum among three numbers.\n    Compares the numbers sequentially to determine the smallest value.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_min = num1\n    if num2 < current_min:\n        current_min = num2\n    if num3 < current_min:\n        current_min = num3\n    return current_min"}
