{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Set all even-positioned bits (0, 2, 4, 6, etc.) to 1 in the given number.\n    Returns the modified integer with even bits set to 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a mask with all even bits set (0x55555555... pattern).\n    # This mask effectively covers bits up to 64-bit integers.\n    even_bit_mask = 0x5555555555555555\n\n    # Use a bitwise OR operation to set all even bits in the number to 1,\n    # without affecting the odd-positioned bits.\n    return number | even_bit_mask"}
