{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(input_list: list) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of unique tuples in a list, treating tuples with the same elements\n    in different orders as identical by normalizing their order.\n    Returns a dictionary mapping normalized tuples to their counts.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def normalize_tuple(t: tuple) -> tuple:\n        \"\"\"\n        Normalizes a tuple by sorting its elements.\n        This ensures tuples like (3, 1) and (1, 3) become (1, 3).\n        \"\"\"\n        return tuple(sorted(t))\n\n    counts = {}\n    for original_tuple in input_list:\n        normalized_tuple = normalize_tuple(original_tuple)\n        counts[normalized_tuple] = counts.get(normalized_tuple, 0) + 1\n\n    return counts"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(tuple_list: list) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of each unique tuple, treating order-independent tuples as equivalent.\n    Normalizes tuples by sorting their elements to ensure consistent keys.\n    \"\"\"\n    def normalize_tuple(t: tuple) -> tuple:\n        \"\"\"Helper to normalize a tuple by sorting its elements.\"\"\"\n        return tuple(sorted(t))\n\n    counts = {}\n    for item in tuple_list:\n        normalized_item = normalize_tuple(item)\n        counts[normalized_item] = counts.get(normalized_item, 0) + 1\n    return counts"}
