{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A bitonic subsequence first increases and then decreases.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return array[0]\n\n    # Calculate increasing_sums[i]: maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index i\n    increasing_sums = list(array)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                increasing_sums[i] = max(increasing_sums[i], increasing_sums[j] + array[i])\n\n    # Calculate decreasing_sums[i]: maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at index i\n    decreasing_sums = list(array)\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                decreasing_sums[i] = max(decreasing_sums[i], decreasing_sums[j] + array[i])\n\n    # Combine increasing_sums and decreasing_sums to find the maximum bitonic sum\n    # Subtract array[i] once because it is counted in both increasing_sums[i] and decreasing_sums[i]\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = increasing_sums[i] + decreasing_sums[i] - array[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A bitonic sequence is first increasing and then decreasing, and can also be purely increasing or purely decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return array[0]\n\n    # Calculate LIS sums ending at each index.\n    # inc_sums[i] is the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at array[i].\n    inc_sums = list(array)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                inc_sums[i] = max(inc_sums[i], inc_sums[j] + array[i])\n\n    # Calculate LDS sums starting at each index.\n    # dec_sums[i] is the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at array[i].\n    dec_sums = list(array)\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):  # Iterate from second to last element backwards\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):  # Look for elements to the right of i\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                dec_sums[i] = max(dec_sums[i], dec_sums[j] + array[i])\n\n    # Combine LIS and LDS sums to find the maximum bitonic subsequence sum.\n    # For each element `array[i]` as a potential peak, its sum is `inc_sums[i] + dec_sums[i] - array[i]`.\n    max_bitonic_sum = float('-inf')\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, inc_sums[i] + dec_sums[i] - array[i])\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum\n```"}
