{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    This uses a dynamic programming approach to fill a DP table.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence\n    # for the substring s[i...j]. It is initialized with 0s.\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromic subsequences of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the table for lengths from 2 to n.\n    # `length` represents the current substring length.\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        # `i` is the starting index of the substring.\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            # `j` is the ending index of the substring.\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If outer characters match, they contribute 2 to the LPS,\n                # plus the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                # If outer characters don't match, the LPS is the maximum\n                # of LPS(s[i+1...j]) and LPS(s[i...j-1]).\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def _validate_input(s: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates the input string parameter.\n    For this problem, any string input is considered valid.\n    \"\"\"\n    return True\n\ndef _handle_edge_cases(s: str) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles edge cases for string length (empty or single character).\n    Returns the LPS length for edge cases, or None if not an edge case.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    return None\n\ndef _calculate_lps_dp(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence using dynamic programming.\n    This function assumes the input string length is guaranteed to be >= 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the LPS for the substring s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the table for lengths from 2 to n\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1 # j is the end index of the current substring s[i...j]\n            \n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters s[i] and s[j] match, they can form the outer pair of a palindrome.\n                # The length is 2 (for s[i] and s[j]) plus the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                # If length is 2, the inner substring is empty (or invalid indices), so add 0.\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + (dp[i + 1][j - 1] if length > 2 else 0)\n            else:\n                # If characters s[i] and s[j] do not match,\n                # the LPS of s[i...j] is the maximum of:\n                # 1. LPS of s[i+1...j] (excluding s[i])\n                # 2. LPS of s[i...j-1] (excluding s[j])\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]\n\ndef lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    It uses helper functions for input validation, edge case handling, and dynamic programming.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(s)\n\n    edge_case_result = _handle_edge_cases(s)\n    if edge_case_result is not None:\n        return edge_case_result\n    \n    return _calculate_lps_dp(s)"}
