{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\n\ndef convert(input_number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Convert complex number to polar coordinates.\n\n    Args:\n        input_number: complex or real number\n\n    Returns:\n        tuple: (magnitude, angle) where magnitude >= 0 and angle in radians\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(input_number, (int, float)):\n        z = complex(input_number, 0)\n    else:\n        z = input_number\n\n    magnitude = math.sqrt(z.real**2 + z.imag**2)\n    angle = math.atan2(z.imag, z.real)\n\n    return (magnitude, angle)"}
