{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Union, Tuple\n\ndef convert(input: Union[int, float, complex]) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Convert complex number to polar coordinates.\n\n    Args:\n        input: Number to convert (int, float, or complex)\n    \"\"\"\n    complex_num = complex(input)\n    real_part = complex_num.real\n    imag_part = complex_num.imag\n\n    magnitude = math.sqrt(real_part**2 + imag_part**2)\n    angle = math.atan2(imag_part, real_part)\n\n    return (magnitude, angle)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers strictly less than the given non-negative number.\n    Uses an optimized primality test for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_prime(n):\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper function to check if a number is prime.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n < 2:\n            return False\n        if n == 2:\n            return True\n        if n % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= n:\n            if n % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(2, number):\n        if _is_prime(i):\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
