{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Maximizes corresponding elements between two tuples of tuples.\n    Returns a new tuple containing the maximum values from each comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_pairs = []\n    for pair1, pair2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        max_first = max(pair1[0], pair2[0])\n        max_second = max(pair1[1], pair2[1])\n        result_pairs.append((max_first, max_second))\n    return tuple(result_pairs)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares two tuples of nested tuples element-wise and returns a new tuple\n    containing the maximum values at each corresponding position.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        # Extract corresponding nested tuples\n        nested_tuple1 = tuple1[i]\n        nested_tuple2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        # Compare first elements and find maximum\n        max_first = max(nested_tuple1[0], nested_tuple2[0])\n        # Compare second elements and find maximum\n        max_second = max(nested_tuple1[1], nested_tuple2[1])\n\n        # Create the new nested tuple with maximums\n        result.append((max_first, max_second))\n    \n    return tuple(result)"}
