{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(array: list[int], array_length: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in an array repeated k times.\n    Applies Kadane's algorithm considering array repetitions and total sum.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def kadane(arr_input: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper function to find the maximum contiguous subarray sum.\"\"\"\n        if not arr_input:\n            return 0  # Max sum of an empty array is 0.\n\n        max_so_far = arr_input[0]\n        current_max = arr_input[0]\n\n        for i in range(1, len(arr_input)):\n            current_max = max(arr_input[i], current_max + arr_input[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n        return max_so_far\n\n    if array_length == 0 or k == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return kadane(array)\n\n    # For k > 1\n    total_sum = sum(array)\n    \n    # Calculate max sum for the array repeated twice.\n    # This covers subarrays completely within one copy, or spanning two copies.\n    extended_array = array + array\n    max_sum_two_copies = kadane(extended_array)\n\n    if total_sum > 0:\n        # If the total sum of the original array is positive,\n        # we can potentially increase the sum by including (k-2) full copies.\n        return max_sum_two_copies + (k - 2) * total_sum\n    else:\n        # If the total sum is non-positive,\n        # adding more full copies beyond two will not increase the sum.\n        # The maximum sum will be found within at most two copies.\n        return max_sum_two_copies"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(array: list[int], array_length: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous array in the modified array,\n    formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to find the maximum subarray sum using Kadane's algorithm.\n    def kadane(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        max_so_far = float('-inf')\n        current_max = 0\n        all_negative = True\n        max_val = float('-inf') # To store the largest single element if all are negative\n\n        for x in arr:\n            if x >= 0:\n                all_negative = False\n            max_val = max(max_val, x)\n\n            current_max += x\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n            if current_max < 0:\n                current_max = 0\n        \n        # If all numbers are negative, the max subarray sum is the largest single number.\n        if all_negative:\n            return max_val\n        return max_so_far\n\n    # Handle edge cases for k or empty array.\n    if k == 0 or not array or array_length == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate properties of the single original array.\n    total_sum = sum(array)\n\n    # Calculate max prefix sum.\n    max_prefix_sum = float('-inf')\n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    for x in array:\n        current_prefix_sum += x\n        max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, current_prefix_sum)\n    \n    # Calculate max suffix sum.\n    max_suffix_sum = float('-inf')\n    current_suffix_sum = 0\n    for x in reversed(array):\n        current_suffix_sum += x\n        max_suffix_sum = max(max_suffix_sum, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    # Maximum subarray sum for a single instance of the array.\n    max_sum_single = kadane(array)\n\n    # If k is 1, the result is simply the max sum within the single array.\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_sum_single\n\n    # For k > 1, consider subarrays that span across multiple repetitions.\n    # Initialize overall max sum with the max sum from a single array.\n    max_overall_sum = max_sum_single\n\n    # Case 1: Subarray spans across two instances (max suffix of first + max prefix of second).\n    max_overall_sum = max(max_overall_sum, max_suffix_sum + max_prefix_sum)\n\n    # Case 2: Subarray spans across more than two instances.\n    # This involves max suffix, (k-2) full array sums, and max prefix.\n    # This is only beneficial if the total sum of the array is positive.\n    if total_sum > 0:\n        max_overall_sum = max(max_overall_sum, max_suffix_sum + (k - 2) * total_sum + max_prefix_sum)\n    \n    return max_overall_sum\n```"}
