{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(array: list[int], length: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from the prefix up to index i,\n    mandatorily including the element at index k (where k > i).\n    \"\"\"\n    # dp[p] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at array[p] for p <= i.\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    # Calculate dp values for the prefix array[0...i]\n    for p in range(i + 1):\n        dp[p] = array[p]  # Initialize with the element itself as a subsequence\n        for j in range(p):\n            if array[p] > array[j]:\n                dp[p] = max(dp[p], dp[j] + array[p])\n\n    # Find the maximum sum from dp[p] that can validly precede array[k]\n    max_sum_prefix_component = 0\n    for p in range(i + 1):\n        if array[p] < array[k]:\n            max_sum_prefix_component = max(max_sum_prefix_component, dp[p])\n\n    # The total maximum sum is the best prefix component found plus array[k]\n    return max_sum_prefix_component + array[k]"}
