{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of all individual digits from each number in a given list.\n    Returns the total sum as a single integer value.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _extract_digits(number: int) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Extracts individual digits from a single number.\n        Returns a list of individual digits.\n        \"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return [0]\n        \n        digits = []\n        for digit_char in str(number):\n            digits.append(int(digit_char))\n        return digits\n\n    def _validate_input(numbers: List[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates input list contains only non-negative integers.\n        Returns True if valid, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        for num in numbers:\n            # Type checking is explicitly forbidden by instructions, assume int input.\n            if num < 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    if not _validate_input(numbers):\n        # If input validation fails (e.g., contains negative numbers), return 0.\n        return 0 \n    \n    total_sum = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        digits = _extract_digits(num)\n        total_sum += sum(digits)\n        \n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of all individual digits for each number in a given list.\n    Negative signs are ignored during digit extraction.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_digit_sum = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        # Convert the number to its absolute string representation to extract digits.\n        for digit_char in str(abs(number)):\n            total_digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n    return total_digit_sum"}
