{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "def min_val(input_list: list) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum numeric value in a heterogeneous list, ignoring non-numeric elements.\n    Handles both integers and floating-point numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_numeric_value = None\n\n    for item in input_list:\n        if isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            if min_numeric_value is None:\n                min_numeric_value = item\n            elif item < min_numeric_value:\n                min_numeric_value = item\n    return min_numeric_value"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "def min_product_tuple(tuples: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum product from pairs of tuples within a given list.\n    Assumes valid input: a non-empty list of two-element numeric tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_product = float('inf')\n\n    for t in tuples:\n        current_product = t[0] * t[1]\n        if current_product < min_product:\n            min_product = current_product\n            \n    return min_product"}
