{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(arr: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the pair with highest product from given array of integers.\n    It iterates through all unique pairs and calculates their product to find the maximum.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_product = float('-inf')\n    result_pair = None\n\n    # Generate all pairs and find the maximum product\n    for i in range(len(arr)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(arr)):\n            product = arr[i] * arr[j]\n            if product > max_product:\n                max_product = product\n                result_pair = (arr[i], arr[j])\n\n    return result_pair"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(array: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of integers with the highest product from a given array.\n    It considers products of the two largest and two smallest numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Sort the array to efficiently find the largest and smallest elements.\n    array.sort()\n\n    # Calculate the product of the two largest numbers.\n    prod_of_largest_two = array[-1] * array[-2]\n    pair_of_largest_two = (array[-2], array[-1])\n\n    # Calculate the product of the two smallest (most negative) numbers.\n    prod_of_smallest_two = array[0] * array[1]\n    pair_of_smallest_two = (array[0], array[1])\n\n    # Return the pair that yielded the highest product.\n    if prod_of_largest_two >= prod_of_smallest_two:\n        return pair_of_largest_two\n    else:\n        return pair_of_smallest_two"}
