{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "# Helper function: Swaps two elements in an array.\ndef _swap_elements(arr: list[int], i: int, j: int) -> None:\n    arr[i], arr[j] = arr[j], arr[i]\n\n# Helper function: Calculates a gap sequence for Shell Sort.\ndef _calculate_gap_sequence(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    gaps = []\n    # Start with a common initial gap and reduce by half.\n    gap = n // 2\n    while gap > 0:\n        gaps.append(gap)\n        gap //= 2\n    return gaps\n\n# Helper function: Performs an insertion sort on a sub-array defined by the gap.\ndef _insertion_sort_with_gap(arr: list[int], gap: int) -> None:\n    n = len(arr)\n    for i in range(gap, n):\n        # Store arr[i] in temp and make a hole at position i.\n        temp = arr[i]\n        j = i\n        # Shift earlier gap-sorted elements up until the correct position for temp is found.\n        while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n            arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n            j -= gap\n        # Put temp (the original arr[i]) in its correct position.\n        arr[j] = temp\n\ndef shell_sort(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts the given array using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted array without modifying the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Handle edge cases for empty or single-element arrays.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return arr[:]\n\n    # Create a mutable copy of the input array to sort.\n    sorted_arr = arr[:]\n\n    # Calculate the sequence of gaps.\n    gaps = _calculate_gap_sequence(n)\n\n    # Perform gapped insertion sort for each gap in the sequence.\n    for gap in gaps:\n        _insertion_sort_with_gap(sorted_arr, gap)\n\n    return sorted_arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef shell_sort(array: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers in ascending order using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    Creates a new sorted list, leaving the original array unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _generate_gap_sequence(n: int) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Generates Knuth's gap sequence (3k+1) for shell sort.\"\"\"\n        gaps = []\n        h = 1\n        while h < n:\n            gaps.append(h)\n            h = h * 3 + 1\n        return gaps[::-1] # Return in descending order\n\n    def _insertion_sort_with_gap(arr: List[int], gap: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Performs insertion sort on elements separated by the specified gap.\"\"\"\n        n = len(arr)\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift elements that are greater than temp to the right\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return array[:] # Return a copy for immutability\n\n    arr_copy = array[:] # Create a copy to preserve the original array\n\n    gaps = _generate_gap_sequence(n)\n\n    for gap in gaps:\n        _insertion_sort_with_gap(arr_copy, gap)\n\n    return arr_copy"}
