{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "```python\ndef combinations_list(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all possible combinations (power set) of elements from the input list.\n    The combinations are generated based on binary representation and match the assertion's specific element order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    all_combinations = []\n\n    # Iterate from 0 to 2^n - 1, where each number represents a unique combination.\n    # (1 << n) is equivalent to 2**n.\n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        current_combination = []\n        # Check each bit of 'i' to determine which elements to include.\n        for j in range(n):\n            # If the j-th bit of 'i' is set (i.e., it's 1), include the j-th element.\n            if (i >> j) & 1:\n                current_combination.append(input_list[j])\n        \n        # The assertion output requires elements within a combination to be in\n        # reverse order of their appearance in the original input_list indices.\n        all_combinations.append(current_combination[::-1])\n\n    return all_combinations\n```"}
