{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "def combinations_list(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Generate all possible combinations of input list elements in binary counting order.\n\n    Each combination's elements maintain relative order but are added based on bit position from most to least significant.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    all_combinations = []\n\n    # Iterate from 0 to 2^n - 1 to generate all possible binary masks\n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        current_combination = []\n        # For each mask, iterate through the elements from right to left (most significant bit to least significant bit)\n        # to construct the combination in the specified order.\n        for j in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n            # Check if the j-th bit is set in the current mask 'i'\n            if (i >> j) & 1:\n                current_combination.append(input_list[j])\n        all_combinations.append(current_combination)\n\n    return all_combinations"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product subarray within a given array.\n    Uses dynamic programming to handle positive, negative, and zero elements efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    min_ending_here = arr[0]\n    max_ending_here = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        num = arr[i]\n\n        # Store max_ending_here before it potentially changes,\n        # as it's needed for min_ending_here calculation.\n        temp_max_ending_here = max_ending_here\n\n        # Update max_ending_here: can be the number itself, or number multiplied by\n        # previous max or min ending here (to handle negative numbers).\n        max_ending_here = max(num, temp_max_ending_here * num, min_ending_here * num)\n        # Update min_ending_here: similarly, can be the number itself, or number multiplied by\n        # previous max or min ending here.\n        min_ending_here = min(num, temp_max_ending_here * num, min_ending_here * num)\n\n        # Update the overall maximum product found across all subarrays.\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
