{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def normalize_tuple(t: tuple) -> frozenset:\n    \"\"\"Converts a tuple to a frozenset for order-independent comparison.\"\"\"\n    return frozenset(t)\n\ndef tuple_intersection(list1: list, list2: list) -> set:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the intersection of tuples between two lists, irrespective of element order within tuples.\n    Returns a set of tuples where elements within each tuple are sorted for consistent representation.\n    \"\"\"\n    normalized_set1 = {normalize_tuple(t) for t in list1}\n    normalized_set2 = {normalize_tuple(t) for t in list2}\n\n    common_normalized_elements = normalized_set1.intersection(normalized_set2)\n\n    # Convert frozensets back to sorted tuples for the final output\n    result_set = {tuple(sorted(fs)) for fs in common_normalized_elements}\n    return result_set"}
