{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def tuple_intersection(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the tuple intersection of elements in the given tuple list irrespective of their order.\n    Returns a set of matching tuples from the first list.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _normalize_tuple(t):\n        \"\"\"Converts a tuple to a frozenset for order-independent comparison.\"\"\"\n        return frozenset(t)\n\n    def _find_matches(input_list1, input_list2):\n        \"\"\"Identifies matching tuples between two lists, preserving original form from the first list.\"\"\"\n        normalized_set2 = {_normalize_tuple(t) for t in input_list2}\n        result_matches = set()\n\n        for t1 in input_list1:\n            if _normalize_tuple(t1) in normalized_set2:\n                result_matches.add(t1)\n        return result_matches\n\n    return _find_matches(list1, list2)"}
