{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "def digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the per-digit absolute differences between two integers.\n    The shorter number is implicitly padded with leading zeros for comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    str_num1 = str(abs(num1))\n    str_num2 = str(abs(num2))\n\n    max_len = max(len(str_num1), len(str_num2))\n\n    # Pad the shorter string with leading zeros to match the length of the longer string\n    padded_str_num1 = str_num1.zfill(max_len)\n    padded_str_num2 = str_num2.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_distance = 0\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit1 = int(padded_str_num1[i])\n        digit2 = int(padded_str_num2[i])\n        total_distance += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    return total_distance"}
