{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "def digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of per-digit absolute differences between two integers.\n    Handles integers of different lengths by padding the shorter number with leading zeros.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def extract_digits(number: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Extracts individual digits from an integer into a list, most significant first.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return [0]\n        digits = []\n        # Use absolute value for digit extraction to handle negative numbers\n        abs_number = abs(number)\n        while abs_number > 0:\n            digits.append(abs_number % 10)\n            abs_number //= 10\n        return digits[::-1]  # Reverse to get most significant digit first\n\n    def calculate_differences(digits1: list[int], digits2: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates absolute differences between corresponding digit pairs.\"\"\"\n        len1 = len(digits1)\n        len2 = len(digits2)\n        max_len = max(len1, len2)\n\n        # Pad shorter list with leading zeros to match length\n        padded_digits1 = [0] * (max_len - len1) + digits1\n        padded_digits2 = [0] * (max_len - len2) + digits2\n\n        differences = []\n        for i in range(max_len):\n            differences.append(abs(padded_digits1[i] - padded_digits2[i]))\n        return differences\n\n    def sum_differences(differences: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Sums all difference values to produce the final result.\"\"\"\n        return sum(differences)\n\n    digits1 = extract_digits(num1)\n    digits2 = extract_digits(num2)\n\n    diffs = calculate_differences(digits1, digits2)\n\n    return sum_differences(diffs)"}
