{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum(arr, length):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of the largest contiguous sublist in the given list using Kadane's algorithm.\n    It efficiently calculates the maximum sum in O(n) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize max_so_far and current_max with the first element of the array.\n    # This initialization correctly handles cases where all numbers are negative.\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    current_max = arr[0]\n\n    # Iterate through the array starting from the second element.\n    for i in range(1, length):\n        # For each element, decide whether to extend the previous subarray or start a new one.\n        # current_max stores the maximum sum of a subarray ending at the current position 'i'.\n        current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n\n        # Update max_so_far if the current maximum sum ending at 'i' is greater than the\n        # overall maximum sum found so far.\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/562", "solution": "def Find_Max_Length(sublists: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest sublist within a list of sublists.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_len = 0\n    for sublist in sublists:\n        current_len = len(sublist)\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n    return max_len"}
