{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "def merge(input_list: list[list]) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transposes a list of two-element sublists into two separate lists.\n    The first output list contains all first elements, and the second contains all second elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return [[], []]\n\n    # Use zip(*input_list) to transpose the list of lists.\n    # This takes the first elements of all sublists, then the second elements, etc.\n    # Since each sublist has two elements, it will result in two tuples.\n    transposed_tuples = zip(*input_list)\n    \n    # Convert the tuples back into lists as required by the output format.\n    return [list(elements) for elements in transposed_tuples]"}
