{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def find_kth_element(arr1, arr2, k):\n    \"\"\"Finds the k-th smallest element (1-indexed) from two sorted arrays.\"\"\"\n    m, n = len(arr1), len(arr2)\n    idx1, idx2 = 0, 0 \n\n    while True:\n        # If arr1 is exhausted, the k-th element must be in arr2.\n        if idx1 == m:\n            return arr2[idx2 + k - 1]\n        # If arr2 is exhausted, the k-th element must be in arr1.\n        if idx2 == n:\n            return arr1[idx1 + k - 1]\n        # If k is 1, the k-th element is the minimum of the current first elements.\n        if k == 1:\n            return min(arr1[idx1], arr2[idx2])\n\n        # Calculate indices to compare, taking approximately k/2 elements from each array.\n        k_half = k // 2\n        new_idx1 = min(idx1 + k_half, m)\n        new_idx2 = min(idx2 + k_half, n)\n        \n        val1 = arr1[new_idx1 - 1]\n        val2 = arr2[new_idx2 - 1]\n\n        # Discard elements from the array whose chosen element is smaller or equal.\n        if val1 <= val2:\n            k -= (new_idx1 - idx1)\n            idx1 = new_idx1\n        else: # val2 < val1\n            k -= (new_idx2 - idx2)\n            idx2 = new_idx2\n\ndef get_median(list1, list2, size):\n    \"\"\"Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\"\"\"\n    # The total number of elements is 2 * size.\n    # The median is the average of the size-th and (size+1)-th elements (1-indexed).\n    \n    # Find the size-th element (1-indexed).\n    median1 = find_kth_element(list1, list2, size)\n    # Find the (size+1)-th element (1-indexed).\n    median2 = find_kth_element(list1, list2, size + 1)\n    \n    return (median1 + median2) / 2.0"}
