{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate: tuple) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all adjacent coordinates in a 3x3 grid centered on the given coordinate,\n    including the center itself, ordered as specified by the assertion.\n    \"\"\"\n    cx, cy = coordinate\n    result = []\n    # Iterate through x-offsets, then y-offsets, to match the assertion's desired output order.\n    for dx in range(-1, 2):  # Offsets for x-coordinate: -1, 0, 1\n        for dy in range(-1, 2):  # Offsets for y-coordinate: -1, 0, 1\n            result.append([cx + dx, cy + dy])\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple: tuple) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all 9 adjacent coordinates (including the center) for a given coordinate.\n    Coordinates are returned in row-major order as a list of lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate_tuple\n    adjacent_coords = []\n\n    # Iterate through x-offsets (-1, 0, 1) and y-offsets (-1, 0, 1)\n    # This ensures row-major order: first all coordinates for x-1, then x, then x+1\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            new_x = x + dx\n            new_y = y + dy\n            adjacent_coords.append([new_x, new_y])\n\n    return adjacent_coords"}
