{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the path with the maximum average cost from the top-left to the bottom-right cell\n    in a square matrix, moving only right or down.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = len(matrix)\n    \n    # Initialize max_average to a very small number to ensure any valid average is greater\n    max_average = -float('inf')\n\n    # Define the recursive DFS helper function\n    def dfs(r: int, c: int, current_sum: float, current_length: int):\n        nonlocal max_average  # Allow modification of max_average from the outer scope\n\n        # Base case: out of bounds\n        if r >= N or c >= N:\n            return\n\n        # Add current cell's cost and increment length for the current path\n        current_sum += matrix[r][c]\n        current_length += 1\n\n        # Base case: Reached the bottom-right cell\n        if r == N - 1 and c == N - 1:\n            max_average = max(max_average, current_sum / current_length)\n            return\n\n        # Recursive calls: explore moving down and moving right\n        dfs(r + 1, c, current_sum, current_length)  # Move down\n        dfs(r, c + 1, current_sum, current_length)  # Move right\n\n    # Start DFS from the top-left cell (0, 0) with initial sum and length of 0.\n    # The cost of the (0,0) cell will be added within the first call to dfs.\n    dfs(0, 0, 0.0, 0)\n\n    return max_average"}
