{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst: list, positions: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of positions.\n    Returns a new list with the rotated elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    n = len(lst)\n    effective_positions = positions % n\n\n    # Elements from the end that move to the front\n    rotated_part = lst[-effective_positions:]\n    # Remaining elements that follow\n    remaining_part = lst[:-effective_positions]\n\n    return rotated_part + remaining_part"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, positions: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items, returning a new list.\n    Handles empty lists and rotation counts larger than list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate the effective number of positions to rotate\n    effective_positions = positions % n\n\n    # Slice the list and concatenate the parts\n    # The last 'effective_positions' elements become the new beginning\n    # The remaining elements follow\n    return input_list[-effective_positions:] + input_list[:-effective_positions]"}
