{"task_id": "Mbpp/759", "solution": "def is_decimal(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given string is a decimal number with exactly 2 decimal places.\n    The string must represent a positive number with at least one digit before the decimal point.\n    \"\"\"\n    if input_string.count('.') != 1:\n        return False\n\n    integer_part, decimal_part = input_string.split('.')\n\n    if not integer_part or not integer_part.isdigit():\n        return False\n\n    if len(decimal_part) != 2 or not decimal_part.isdigit():\n        return False\n\n    return True"}
