{"task_id": "Mbpp/777", "solution": "def count_elements(input_list: list) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Counts occurrences of each element in the input list.\n    Returns a dictionary mapping elements to their counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for element in input_list:\n        counts[element] = counts.get(element, 0) + 1\n    return counts\n\ndef filter_unique_elements(element_counts: dict) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Filters distinct elements from a count dictionary.\n    Returns a list of all unique values present in the original list.\n    \"\"\"\n    return list(element_counts.keys())\n\ndef calculate_sum(unique_elements: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of a list of numbers.\n    Returns the total sum of all elements in the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(unique_elements)\n\ndef find_sum(input_list: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the sum of non-repeated elements in a given list.\n    Non-repeated elements are interpreted as unique *values* in the list to match the provided assertion.\n    \"\"\"\n    element_counts = count_elements(input_list)\n    unique_elements = filter_unique_elements(element_counts)\n    total_sum = calculate_sum(unique_elements)\n    return total_sum"}
