{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(sorted_array: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a specified value in sorted order.\n    Returns the index where the target should be inserted to maintain sorted order,\n    ensuring it's to the right of any existing equal elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    left, right = 0, len(sorted_array)\n\n    while left < right:\n        mid = left + (right - left) // 2\n        if sorted_array[mid] <= target:\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:\n            right = mid\n    return left"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(array: list, target_value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the rightmost insertion point for a specified value in a sorted array.\n    Uses binary search to achieve O(log n) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] <= target_value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n            \n    return low"}
