{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array, target):\n  \"\"\"\n  Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n  Returns the index of the last occurrence, or -1 if the element is not found.\n  \"\"\"\n  low = 0\n  high = len(array) - 1\n  result = -1\n\n  while low <= high:\n    mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n    if array[mid] == target:\n      result = mid      # Found a potential last occurrence\n      low = mid + 1     # Try to find a later occurrence in the right half\n    elif array[mid] < target:\n      low = mid + 1\n    else:\n      high = mid - 1\n\n  return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array: list, target_element) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the zero-based index of the last occurrence, or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] == target_element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find further occurrences on the right\n        elif array[mid] < target_element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n            \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/791", "solution": "def _is_tuple_element(element: any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an element is a tuple.\"\"\"\n    return type(element) is tuple\n\ndef remove_nested(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes nested tuples from the given tuple.\n    Preserves the order of non-tuple elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for element in input_tuple:\n        if not _is_tuple_element(element):\n            result.append(element)\n    return tuple(result)"}
