{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l, r):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are positive integers (1, 2, 3,...).\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Ensure the starting point is at least 1, as natural numbers start from 1.\n    start = max(1, l)\n\n    for num in range(start, r + 1):\n        if num % 2 != 0:  # Check if the number is odd\n            total_sum += num\n            \n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit number to the left by d positions.\n    Bits shifted off the left end reappear on the right end.\n    \"\"\"\n    N_BITS = 32\n    # Ensure d is within the range [0, N_BITS-1]\n    d = d % N_BITS\n\n    # Perform the left rotation\n    # Part 1: Bits shifted to the left within the 32-bit boundary\n    part1 = (number << d)\n\n    # Part 2: Bits that wrapped around from the left to the right\n    part2 = (number >> (N_BITS - d))\n\n    # Combine the two parts using bitwise OR\n    rotated_number = part1 | part2\n\n    # Mask the result to ensure it remains a 32-bit number\n    return rotated_number & ((1 << N_BITS) - 1)"}
