{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotate left bits by d bits for a 32-bit number.\n    This function performs a circular left shift on the given integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    BITS = 32\n    # Normalize the rotation distance to be within [0, BITS-1].\n    d = d % BITS\n\n    # Perform the left circular rotation using bitwise operations.\n    # The first part shifts bits left, and the mask ensures it remains 32-bit.\n    # The second part captures bits that wrap around from the left.\n    return ((number << d) & 0xFFFFFFFF) | (number >> (BITS - d))"}
